#~ "database. Click a column heading to "
#~ "sort the table by the values "
#~ "within the column click again to "
#~ "reverse the sort order.<br/><br/><b>Schema:</b> "
#~ "This column identifies the schema in "
#~ "which the table resides.<br/><b>Table "
#~ "Name:</b> This column identifies the "
#~ "name of the table.<br/><b>Scans:</b> The "
#~ "number of scans performed on the "
#~ "table.<br/><b>Rows Read:</b> The number of "
#~ "rows read from the specified "
#~ "table.<br/><b>Index Scans:</b> The number of"
#~ " index scans performed on the "
#~ "specified table.<br/><b>Index Rows Read:</b> "
#~ "The number of rows read during "
#~ "index scans on the specified "
#~ "table.<br/><b>Rows Inserted:</b> The number of"
#~ " rows inserted into the specified "
#~ "table.<br/><b>Rows Updated:</b> The number of"
#~ " rows updated in the specified "
#~ "table.<br/><b>Rows Deleted:</b> The number of"
#~ " rows deleted from the specified "
#~ "table.<br/><b>Hot Rows Updated:</b> The number"
#~ " of hot row updates into the "
#~ "table when a hot row update "
#~ "occurs, the new row occupies the "
#~ "same page as the previous "
#~ "row.<br/><b>Total Rows:</b> The number of "
#~ "total rows in the table.<br/><b>Dead "
#~ "Rows:</b> The number of rows that "
#~ "have been deleted, but have not "
